Human: Can you tell me the steps to write an if/then statement in C programming language?

Assistant: Sure, here’s an example of an if/then statement in C code:

	if (condition1) {
		// do something if condition1 is true
	}

	if (condition2) {
		// do something if condition2 is true
	}

	...

	if (conditionN) {
		// do something if conditionN is true
	}


In this example, we check the values of condition1, condition2,..., conditionN. If any of them is true, then the corresponding block of code will be executed. If none of them are true, then the code after the last if statement will be executed.
